## GAME INTEGRATION STARTED (5 Oct 2026, night) - EWS_with_Build.html
Files: EWS_with_Build.html (game + Build module), EWS_ORIGINAL_BACKUP.html (untouched copy of Tools/Equestrian_Wasteland_Sim.json, an HTML file). The game ALREADY had its own shell (mode orb = pause toggle, time orb, cinematic orb, revolver hub with 6 bullets, sheets, fluid/peristalsis, cutaway, gestation). Nothing in it was edited; a marked module was appended before </body>.
What the module does: adds a Build orb (hammer, above the pause orb). Tap = full-screen overlay of the ST3D editor (embedded in the file as base64, shown in an iframe), game time paused (simSpeed 0). In the overlay the editor's mode orb is the exit: tap it to return to Live. On exit, if the body was changed, the editor posts its nodes to the game; the game rebuilds its body balls from them and saves to localStorage key ews.body.nodes (restored at game start and re-sent to the editor next time Build opens).
Axis map editor -> game: x->x, y(side)->z, z(up)->y; scale [sx,sy,sz] -> [sx,sz,sy]. 1:1 units. Rotation ignored. Needs balls named chest and rear (game code uses them) or the change is refused with a message.
