## RAGDOLL MODULE ADDED TO THE GAME (5 Oct 2026, night) - inside EWS_with_Build.html
Owner requirement (stated): ALL collision is ragdoll, interactable mesh physics (collide with surfaces and other avatars, grab and drop, object travels mouth -> throat -> stomach -> intestine -> out the back). Decision recorded earlier: custom position-based (Verlet/PBD) solver on node spheres. pony_ragdoll_lab.html is the 2D-canvas prototype; the module is its port into the game's three.js scene.
Built: Ragdoll orb (bone icon, left, above the Build orb) cycles Off -> Standing physics (springs back to the rest pose, can be pushed) -> Free ragdoll. Verlet particles = the game's body balls (follows Build edits; parent links from editor nodes if present, else name rules), rigid parent links + cross links + soft min-distance limits, ball-ball and ground collision, gravity, damping. Drag any ball with a finger (plane facing the camera); that touch is swallowed so it does not walk or orbit. Organ group follows the chest/rear axis (rotation + offset). Pauses while Build is open.
Tested headless with stubs only: free fall settles on ground (balls y 0.08-0.42), rigid links stay within 0.5%, no NaN, standing mode returns near rest, Off restores positions. NOT run in a browser or on iPad; the touch grab path (raycast + plane) is completely untested.
NOT built (do next, in this order): (1) collision with world objects (props, pool, walls: only the ground exists) and other avatars; (2) the swallow transit through the real tract (mouth -> exit) using the pass-through proof; (3) game walking is still active in ragdoll (tapping ground moves the group); (4) bag pressure/fluids driving ball scale; (5) editor-side preview of ragdoll.

