## BODY MOVEMENT / DYNAMIC MOTION PLAN (owner, 5 Oct 2026, end of night) - NOTE, NOT BUILT
Owner's intent, in his words paraphrased: the ragdoll must give believable natural motion. Flip the pony and she really flips, and gravity settles her flatter onto her back. Pick a pony up and carry her toward something she dislikes and her reaction comes from the physics: quick gravity changes from his hand moves, fluids sloshing inside the body, all of it dynamic, not canned animation. This is meant to LINK to the dynamic response system the Game Master writes (example from owner: if you do not shower, ponies keep their distance; the same layer would make a pony resist/flinch when carried toward something she wants to avoid). Owner says the supporting math ("math you found") and the Game Master rules are in his vault (Google AI Studio / Gemini side); I (this chat's Claude) could NOT see that math: nothing in Tools.zip or the bundle mentions shower/hygiene/avoidance, flipping or sloshing. Ask him to attach the vault file if it is needed. Do not invent it.
What the current ragdoll already gives toward this: real gravity, ball-ball and ground and wall collision, grabbing any ball (so lifting, flipping and dropping are physical), Standing mode spring that returns to pose. Gaps to reach the plan: (1) a pose-spring strength per pony that the Game Master can drive (stiff = tense/resisting, soft = limp; currently fixed 0.05); (2) angular behaviour on flip: balls are unrotated spheres, so a flipped pony has no orientation; add a body frame (chest-rear axis plus a belly/up vector from leg balls) so organs, meshes and the head can rotate with it (organ group already follows the chest-rear axis, belly roll is missing); (3) internal fluid slosh: bag/stomach contents as a damped mass-spring that lags body acceleration and pushes node scale (ties to bag pressure plan and the pass-through proof); (4) an event hook so the Game Master layer can read physics state (held, carried, distance to disliked object, acceleration) and write back (tension, flee direction); (5) arousal-free, adult-characters-only rule for reproductive systems still applies.

